{
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "formats-xml/limits/4301-digit-text-without-a-schema-stays-a-string",
      "spec": "docs/02-document-model.md#24-safety-limits",
      "operation": "parse",
      "purpose": "edge-case",
      "input": {
        "format": "xml",
        "text": "<r><n></n></r>"
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "r",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "n",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": ""
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "comment": "D-28 and C-18: the digit limit binds the schema-directed pretyping of an `integer` leaf and nothing else. With no schema the text is a string of 4 301 characters, no limit applies, and nothing is refused. (The with-schema half, `document.limit.int-digits` at `$.r.n`, is prose only in E-4a: `parse` takes no schema.) Verified live 2026-10-18 at the ports default-branch tips: passes on Python, TypeScript, Rust, Go and Java."
    },
    {
      "name": "formats-xml/limits/non-finite-spellings-stay-strings",
      "spec": "docs/07-codecs-and-deserialization.md#71-two-stages",
      "operation": "parse",
      "purpose": "edge-case",
      "input": {
        "format": "xml",
        "text": "<r><a>NaN</a><b>Infinity</b><c>INF</c><d>-INF</d></r>"
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "r",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "a",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": "NaN"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    "b",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": "Infinity"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    "c",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": "INF"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    "d",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": "-INF"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "comment": "C-18 and C-19: XML has no spelling for a non-finite number, so these are strings (and, against a `number` schema, `materialize.inexact-conversion`). Verified live 2026-10-18 at the ports default-branch tips: passes on Python, TypeScript, Rust, Go and Java."
    }
  ]
